🔄 4. Event Flow (Very Important)
1️⃣ Tenant sends event to your platform

POST /api/events

{
  "eventType": "payment.completed",
  "data": { ... }
}

2️⃣ Your platform stores event in DB

Creates one Event row.

3️⃣ For each webhook endpoint:

Create a Delivery job in BullMQ:

delivery-queue.add("delivery", { eventId, endpointId })

4️⃣ Worker processes job

Fetch event + endpoint

Sign payload with secret

POST to endpoint

Save attempt log

5️⃣ If delivery fails

Worker schedules retry using exponential backoff:

1s → 10s → 30s → 5m → 30m → 2h → Stop

6️⃣ After max retries

Move to Dead Letter Queue
Create DeadLetter record.

7️⃣ Tenant dashboard

Shows:

Successful deliveries

Pending deliveries

Failed ≤ retrying

Dead Letter items

Retry event button

Delivery timelines

