1. Delivery

In a webhook platform, a Delivery represents a single attempt to send a webhook event to a target.

Key points:

Each delivery is tied to a Webhook Event (the payload generated by your system).

Each delivery goes to a Destination (the target URL or endpoint).

Each delivery can succeed, fail, or be retried.


Relationships:

One Event → Many Deliveries
(Same event can be sent to multiple destinations)

One Destination → Many Deliveries
(Same webhook endpoint can receive many events)


A Destination represents a configured target endpoint (URL) where events are delivered.

Key points:

Destinations are reusable: multiple events can be sent to the same endpoint.

Each destination can have configurations like secret keys, headers, or retry policies.

Relationships:

One Destination → Many Deliveries
(Each delivery attempt points to a destination)

. Event → Delivery → Destination Flow

A Webhook Event is generated in the system.

The system looks up all Destinations subscribed to this event.

For each destination, a Delivery is created to track the attempt.

The Delivery records the attempt, status, response, and schedules retries if needed.

